<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resources the shrinker cannot see a reference to, and must keep anyway.

  Flutter's own Gradle plugin turns on both R8 and resource shrinking for the
  release build type — FlutterPlugin.kt sets `isMinifyEnabled = true` and
  `isShrinkResources = true` regardless of what android/app/build.gradle says.
  So a release build IS shrunk, and anything the shrinker can't trace a
  reference to is deleted from the APK.

  ic_stat_nyro is exactly that. Its only reference is the Dart string
  'drawable/ic_stat_nyro' passed to JustAudioBackground.init in lib/main.dart,
  which audio_service resolves at runtime with Resources.getIdentifier(). The
  shrinker's "safe" mode looks for resource-name string constants in Java and
  Kotlin bytecode; this one lives in the AOT snapshot in libapp.so, which it
  cannot read. So the drawable was stripped, getIdentifier() returned 0, and
  the first notification the media session posted threw

      IllegalArgumentException: Invalid notification (no valid small icon)

  on the main thread — killing the app the moment a track started playing, in
  release builds only. Debug builds are not shrunk, which is why it never
  showed up in development.

  Anything else referenced only from Dart by resource name belongs in this
  list too.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_stat_nyro" />
